Cell viability of the membranes was evaluated using the MTT assay. To prepare the samples, they were sterilized by immersion in 60% ethanol and exposure to UV light for one hour. L929 and MG-63 murine fibroblast cell lines, provided by the Cell Bank of the Pasteur Institute of Iran, were used for biological assessment. Cells were cultured in DMEM supplemented with 10% fetal bovine serum (FBS) and 1% streptomycin/penicillin, maintained at 37°C in a humidified atmosphere containing 5% CO₂. A total of 10⁴ cells were seeded onto each sample well, with tissue culture plates (TCP) serving as the control. The cells were cultured over five days, and the culture medium was refreshed on day two. MTT assays were performed on days 1, 3, and 5. On each of these days, the medium was removed, and 100 μL of MTT solution (5 mg/mL) was added to both sample and control wells, followed by a 3-hour incubation. After incubation, the resulting dark blue formazan crystals were dissolved in DMSO, and 100 μL of the resulting solution from each well was transferred to a 96-well plate. The optical density (OD) was measured at 490 nm using a Biorad ELISA reader (USA). Cell viability was then calculated using the following equation [ 37 ,  38 ]. 4 \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
